health care systems are helping us to  live longer healthier lives but as we  live longer in the population ages our  current systems are becoming harder to  afford patients expect more and advance  new treatments and technologies are also  increasingly expensive government  spending on health care and long term  care has been increasing from about 5.7  percent of GDP in the EU in the 80s to  eight point seven percent of GDP in 2015  on current trends this figure could  reach 12.5 percent by 2060 the situation  varies considerably but governments in  the EU on average now spend about  fifteen percent of their budgets on  health care making it the second biggest  item after social protection but there  is plenty we can do to lower costs while  maintaining access to quality care and  improving public health investing more  in disease prevention and promoting good  health could reduce the burden of  preventable diseases investing in  primary care could help citizens stay  healthy and reduce the need for heavy  Hospital based treatments that have a  greater impact on quality of life the  cost of medication can be lowered by  promoting the rational use of medicines  and avoiding over prescription joint  procurement can cut costs significantly  without affecting quality or safety  several countries have agreed to adopt  this approach for medical products  linked to contagious diseases better  coordination between care providers can  empower patients with chronic conditions  to live independently and avoid  unnecessary hospitalization the European  Commission is helping Member States to  meet these challenges by providing  independent advice facilitating  cooperation and offering concrete  solutions these include the EU  health action plan to harness health  tools to improve health care for  patients giving them more control of  their care while bringing down costs and  facilitating cooperation between member  states on the assessments of new  technologies to ensure there are  efficient and cost effective finally the  EU also provides funding for medical  research and structural reforms thereby  proving expertise not only to save money  but making people's lives better the  European economy stronger together  [Music]
 

